\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces End-to-end Binius64 proving cost for $N$ independent $128{\times }128{\to }256$ multiplications, without and with zero knowledge. Each multiplication is composed schoolbook-style from four native $64{\times }64{\to }128$ \texttt  {imul} gates ($4$ MUL and $11$ AND constraints). The ZK path is \emph  {recursive}: it symbolically executes the inner verifier to derive an outer Spartan constraint system, pads it with blinding, and commits through the BaseFold ZK compiler. Its overhead is therefore close to \emph  {additive} rather than multiplicative --- roughly $+430$\,KiB of proof, $+2.4$\,ms of verification and $+20$--$30$\,ms of proving, independent of $N$ --- so the relative cost falls as $N$ grows. Measured on arm64 macOS (NEON+AES, all cores), \texttt  {LOG\_INV\_RATE}${}=1$, Criterion mid-estimates over 10 samples.}}{66}{table.caption.37}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:binius64-bignum128-zk}{{7}{66}{End-to-end Binius64 proving cost for $N$ independent $128{\times }128{\to }256$ multiplications, without and with zero knowledge. Each multiplication is composed schoolbook-style from four native $64{\times }64{\to }128$ \texttt {imul} gates ($4$ MUL and $11$ AND constraints). The ZK path is \emph {recursive}: it symbolically executes the inner verifier to derive an outer Spartan constraint system, pads it with blinding, and commits through the BaseFold ZK compiler. Its overhead is therefore close to \emph {additive} rather than multiplicative --- roughly $+430$\,KiB of proof, $+2.4$\,ms of verification and $+20$--$30$\,ms of proving, independent of $N$ --- so the relative cost falls as $N$ grows. Measured on arm64 macOS (NEON+AES, all cores), \texttt {LOG\_INV\_RATE}${}=1$, Criterion mid-estimates over 10 samples}{table.caption.37}{}}
\newlabel{tab:binius64-bignum128-zk@cref}{{[table][7][]7}{[1][66][]66}{}{}{}}
